# 10 · Platform and Build

## Build Philosophy
- Builds must be reproducible, deterministic, and automatable.
- The same source revision should produce predictable artifacts across environments.

## Environment Management
- Separate local, CI, staging, and production configuration clearly.
- Keep environment-specific values outside source via secure configuration.
- Document required environment variables and defaults.

## CI/CD Baseline
- CI runs format/lint, tests, and packaging steps relevant to the stack.
- Release pipelines are versioned, observable, and auditable.
- Failed deployments must fail fast with actionable diagnostics.

## Artifact and Release Management
- Produce immutable, versioned artifacts.
- Sign artifacts where platform/regulatory requirements apply.
- Keep release notes/changelogs with customer and operator impact.

## Multi-Platform Considerations
- Define supported platform/version matrix explicitly.
- Track and gate platform-specific regressions (mobile/web/desktop/server runtimes).
- Keep platform conditionals minimal and isolated.

## Runtime Readiness
- Health checks and startup validation are required for deployable services/apps.
- Feature flags should support controlled rollout for high-risk changes.
- Rollback or quick-disable path must be documented and tested.

## Observability in Build and Release
- Capture build metadata (commit, version, timestamp, environment).
- Tie deployed artifacts to monitoring dashboards and alert ownership.
